singing the same songs

00:02:11.032 --> 00:02:12.048
"with the same haircut."

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:14.462
But it's just, you got
to have fun as well.

00:02:14.462 --> 00:02:15.295
Write it down.

00:02:15.295 --> 00:02:17.541
Make sure you write it
down and take pictures.

00:02:17.541 --> 00:02:18.578
Make sure it's a journey

00:02:18.578 --> 00:02:22.316
and the journey is way more
important than where you end up.

00:02:22.316 --> 00:02:23.768
That's what you have to remember.

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:26.424
If you want to be a fireman, go and do it.

00:02:26.424 --> 00:02:27.499
If you want to be a ballet dancer,

00:02:27.499 --> 00:02:28.743
then go and be a ballet dancer.

00:02:28.743 --> 00:02:29.673
If you don't believe in yourself,

00:02:29.673 --> 00:02:32.756
then no one else will believe in you.

00:02:33.994 --> 00:02:35.843
It's so important for me
to people to understand

00:02:35.843 --> 00:02:37.550
that I want to be an inspiration.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:41.753
I was bullied as kind of
nine out of ten children are

00:02:41.753 --> 00:02:43.271
and I want to be a role model

00:02:43.271 --> 00:02:45.062
and I think now I'm in the
kind of limelight to go,

00:02:45.062 --> 00:02:46.305
"It's okay,"

00:02:46.305 --> 00:02:48.384
and it's the special
people that are bullied.

00:02:48.384 --> 00:02:50.658
They're the ones that
have something magical

00:02:50.658 --> 00:02:52.855
and it's something that you
can turn into a positive

00:02:52.855 --> 00:02:54.130
and not let it eat you away.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.781
There'll always be someone
that says, "You can't do it."

00:02:56.781 --> 00:02:57.630
There'll always be someone that says,

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:58.977
"I don't believe in you."

00:02:58.977 --> 00:03:01.010
There'll always be someone that
says, "I do believe in you,"

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.328
and there's always someone
that says, "You can do it,"

00:03:03.328 --> 00:03:04.945
and that's the people
that you have to focus on.

00:03:04.945 --> 00:03:06.843
However much people try and
put me down, which they do,

00:03:06.843 --> 00:03:07.676
and they say,

00:03:07.676 --> 00:03:10.067
"Every time I hear your song,
I want to burn my ears,"

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:12.329
I say, "Who's laughing now?"

00:03:12.329 --> 00:03:14.160
I will never surround myself with people

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.543
that tell me I'm perfect

00:03:15.543 --> 00:03:18.612
because I'm not and I don't want to be.

00:03:18.612 --> 00:03:22.322
I'm 23 and sometimes I sing out of tune

00:03:22.322 --> 00:03:25.718
and sometimes I lose weight
and I want to gain weight

00:03:25.718 --> 00:03:27.811
and sometimes I say stuff that I shouldn't

00:03:27.811 --> 00:03:29.340
and sometimes I'm going to make mistakes,

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.253
but life would be boring if you lived it

00:03:31.253 --> 00:03:32.671
like it's going to be written in the paper

00:03:32.671 --> 00:03:34.307
and you don't want it to be.

00:03:34.307 --> 00:03:35.494
(audience cheering)

00:03:35.494 --> 00:03:37.202
So I went and I said,
"Yes, it was out of tune

00:03:37.202 --> 00:03:38.859
"and it was pitchy,

00:03:38.859 --> 00:03:40.995
"but I've never mind
and I'm proud of that."

00:03:40.995 --> 00:03:42.806
I like to read reviews.

00:03:42.806 --> 00:03:44.014
I don't take them in as facts

00:03:44.014 --> 00:03:48.181
because one person's opinion
isn't the epitome of life.

00:03:49.681 --> 00:03:52.439
It's not the definity of my work,

00:03:52.439 --> 00:03:56.044
but I'm very, very interested
to see what people think

00:03:56.044 --> 00:03:58.337
because they notice things
that I may not have noticed.

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:03.039
I've listened to this album
70 times in the last month

00:04:03.039 --> 00:04:07.470
so I'm not hearing things
that other people may notice.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.744
So that's always important for me

00:04:08.744 --> 00:04:10.474
to always try and better myself,

00:04:10.474 --> 00:04:12.180
but listen to the right people.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.647
I have my dream list and
I've ticked a few things off

00:04:14.647 --> 00:04:16.733
and I add things on every day.

00:04:16.733 --> 00:04:18.845
I think life's about dreaming big

00:04:18.845 --> 00:04:22.386
and I think I've realized
if you put your mind to it

00:04:22.386 --> 00:04:24.124
and a lot of people I think seem to think

00:04:24.124 --> 00:04:25.643
I've popped out of nowhere

00:04:25.643 --> 00:04:27.194
and I've been signed for seven years.

00:04:27.194 --> 00:04:29.898
And there've been a lot
of times that I was like,

00:04:29.898 --> 00:04:32.877
"This isn't going to happen,"
and it gets really tough

00:04:32.877 --> 00:04:37.546
and Who You Are, songs like
that, made me carry on.

00:04:37.546 --> 00:04:39.998
I would never, ever base
my career on success

00:04:39.998 --> 00:04:42.081
or number ones or awards.

00:04:43.705 --> 00:04:45.344
It's about being happy

00:04:45.344 --> 00:04:48.574
and I just need to make
sure I'm happy, which I am.

00:04:48.574 --> 00:04:50.274
So we're all good in the 'hood.

00:04:50.274 --> 00:04:53.190
Okay, if you're a teacher at school

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:57.203
and there's 30 teachers
in the, what's it called?

00:04:57.203 --> 00:04:58.789
The teacher's room, what's it called?

00:04:58.789 --> 00:04:59.622
Staff room.

00:04:59.622 --> 00:05:00.455
- [Interviewer] Staff room, yeah.

00:05:00.455 --> 00:05:03.565
- The staff room, and there's
one teacher that hates you.

00:05:03.565 --> 00:05:04.914
That's going to play on your mind.

00:05:04.914 --> 00:05:07.897
Any normal person wouldn't
just be able to go,

00:05:07.897 --> 00:05:09.024
"All these people like me,

00:05:09.024 --> 00:05:10.798
"but there's that one person
that's giving me evils

00:05:10.798 --> 00:05:14.001
"that's not giving me a biscuit."

00:05:14.001 --> 00:05:17.111
It's a normal human thing to
want to be liked by people

00:05:17.111 --> 00:05:20.194
that you don't know why
they don't like you,

00:05:20.194 --> 00:05:23.892
but I've realized (laughs)
I can't keep everybody happy

00:05:23.892 --> 00:05:26.028
and that if everyone was the same,

00:05:26.028 --> 00:05:27.697
then everyone would agree
with the way I live my life,

00:05:27.697 --> 00:05:31.162
but they're not and that's
something you have to accept.

00:05:31.162 --> 00:05:31.995
And they're successful

00:05:31.995 --> 00:05:34.025
so they should just enjoy the people

00:05:34.025 --> 00:05:36.786
that are supporting them always, yeah.

00:05:36.786 --> 00:05:39.666
Every body deals with
criticism in their own way.

00:05:39.666 --> 00:05:40.717
I just have to remember

00:05:40.717 --> 00:05:43.602
that a lot more people have an opinion,

00:05:43.602 --> 00:05:45.615
but everyone feels the same.

00:05:45.615 --> 00:05:48.431
Like if somebody came up to
you in the street and was like,

00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:49.667
"Ugh, look what you're wearing.

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:51.200
"I hate you."

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.690
You wouldn't go, "Thanks,
lovely to meet you."

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.401
Your instinct would be like, "Wait."

00:05:56.401 --> 00:05:57.526
But you have to remember

00:05:57.526 --> 00:05:59.925
that there's no point in
wasting your energy on that

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:02.166
and one of the reasons I
honestly wrote It's My Party

00:06:02.166 --> 00:06:04.522
was to almost verbally try
and give those people a hug

00:06:04.522 --> 00:06:07.166
'cause the people that need
that criticism all the time

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.909
