00:10:40.275 --> 00:10:41.108
I believe in you.

00:10:41.108 --> 00:10:43.067
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:10:43.067 --> 00:10:44.878
and whatever your one word is.

00:10:44.878 --> 00:10:46.468
Much love.

00:10:46.468 --> 00:10:47.968
I'll see you soon.

00:10:53.402 --> 00:10:54.933
- Price Tag's more about

00:10:54.933 --> 00:10:56.514
remember that when you don't have money,

00:10:56.514 --> 00:10:59.923
you don't need to go to a five star hotel

00:10:59.923 --> 00:11:01.771
and be in a Jean-Paul Gaultier dress

00:11:01.771 --> 00:11:03.416
and all this to feel amazing.

00:11:03.416 --> 00:11:06.305
Just have a little
picnic in your front room

00:11:06.305 --> 00:11:08.022
and just remember that
your morals, your beliefs,

00:11:08.022 --> 00:11:09.350
and the people that are
around you are more important

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:11.614
than how much money
you've got in your pocket.

00:11:11.614 --> 00:11:13.192
- So there was a time when you were like,

00:11:13.192 --> 00:11:14.398
"I don't know if this is
ever going to happen."

00:11:14.398 --> 00:11:17.403
- Yeah, I feel like every
time I took a step forward,

00:11:17.403 --> 00:11:19.628
like my foot broke or this
happened or duh duh duh,

00:11:19.628 --> 00:11:21.713
I had a stroke when I was
18, just as I got signed,

00:11:21.713 --> 00:11:23.850
and like it's always kind
of there's been moments

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:24.732
when I'm like, "Argh"

00:11:24.732 --> 00:11:27.159
but nothing that's ever kind of stopped me

00:11:27.159 --> 00:11:28.882
but I felt like,

00:11:28.882 --> 00:11:31.379
obviously my second album
didn't get released in the U.S.

00:11:31.379 --> 00:11:32.523
and that was a big knock back for me

00:11:32.523 --> 00:11:34.177
'cause it just didn't feel right here,

00:11:34.177 --> 00:11:36.036
which is fair and it wasn't my choice,

00:11:36.036 --> 00:11:37.468
but, again, it's frustrating

00:11:37.468 --> 00:11:40.348
because you want all the
fans to grow with you,

00:11:40.348 --> 00:11:44.028
even if it's not what
you feel they might love.

00:11:44.028 --> 00:11:46.236
But I just feel like
where I'm at right now,

00:11:46.236 --> 00:11:49.980
I'm very appreciative,
even what's happened today,

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.788
I never, ever thought I would see my name

00:11:52.788 --> 00:11:55.901
at the top of the iTunes
chart in the U.S. ever,

00:11:55.901 --> 00:11:58.833
like so I'm feeling pretty...

00:11:58.833 --> 00:11:59.887
- [DJ] You're feeling yourself today.

00:11:59.887 --> 00:12:01.887
- No, I feel really like

00:12:03.824 --> 00:12:07.412
1% of artists get to release
a third album, you know,

00:12:07.412 --> 00:12:09.707
like only one person can sit at the top,

00:12:09.707 --> 00:12:11.969
like for that moment,
and so when you have it,

00:12:11.969 --> 00:12:15.790
you just have to enjoy it
and have to appreciate it.

